  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anil Prabhakar Amrutkar vs State Of Maharashtra on 7 June, 2023 Author: Amit Borkar Bench: Amit Borkar 2023:Bhc-As:14979 920-aba1578-2 Agk In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.1578 Of 2023 Anil Prabhakar Amrutkar ... Applicant V/s. The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Mr. Chetan S. Damre for the applicant. Mrs. Rutuja Ambekar, App for the respondent/State. Coram : Amit Borkar, J. Dated : June 7, 2023 P.C.: 1.",
    "facts": "The applicant is seeking relief under Section 438 of the Criminal Procedure Code, 1973 in connection with C.R. No.I-301 of 2023 dated 15 May 2023 for offences punishable under Section 328, 272, 273, 188 read with Section 34 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 and under Section 26, 27, 29, 30, and 59 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006. 2. The case of prosecution in short is that on 15 May 2023 at 17.45 hours they seized huge quantity of pan masala (prohibited substances). Based on statement of person from whose custody banned substances were seized, name of the applicant surfaced. The co-accused stated in his statement, recorded on 15 May 2023, that the applicant along with other two persons are the suppliers of banned substances. Apprehending arrest, the applicant filed application under Section 438 of the Criminal Procedure Code, 1973 before the Sessions Court. The learned Sessions Court rejected the application by order dated 24 May 2023. Aggrieved thereby, the applicant has filed present anticipatory bail application.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned advocate for the applicant submitted that the applicant has not been named in the first information report. He has been falsely implicated. The prohibited substances has been seized and, therefore, custodial interrogation of the applicant is not necessary. He is ready to cooperate with the investigation. 5. Per contra, learned APP submitted that the applicant is in the business of supplying prohibited substances. It is necessary to unearth traces of larger supply of banned substances. He submitted that the coordinate Benches of this Court in case of Sagar Sadashiv Kore v. State of Maharashtra, reported in 2021 SCC OnLine Bom 6568 and in Ankush v. State, thr PSO, reported in 2020 SCC OnLine Bom 11384 refused to grant pre- arrest protection to the applicants therein having similar role attributed to the applicants therein. 6. 7. Learned Single Judge of this Court in Ankush (supra) in paragraph 8 observed thus: \"8. The State Government has exercised, from time to time, the statutory power under the FSS Act to prohibit the manufacture, storage, distribution and transport or sale of tobacco, whether flavoured, scented or mixed with other ingredients such as nicotine, menthol etc.\" 8.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Learned advocate for the applicant submitted that the applicant has not been named in the first information report. He has been falsely implicated. The prohibited substances has been seized and, therefore, custodial interrogation of the applicant is not necessary. He is ready to cooperate with the investigation. 5. Per contra, learned APP submitted that the applicant is in the business of supplying prohibited substances. It is necessary to unearth traces of larger supply of banned substances. He submitted that the coordinate Benches of this Court in case of Sagar Sadashiv Kore v. State of Maharashtra, reported in 2021 SCC OnLine Bom 6568 and in Ankush v. State, thr PSO, reported in 2020 SCC OnLine Bom 11384 refused to grant pre- arrest protection to the applicants therein having similar role attributed to the applicants therein. 6.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "7. Learned Single Judge of this Court in Ankush (supra) in paragraph 8 observed thus: \"8. The State Government has exercised, from time to time, the statutory power under the FSS Act to prohibit the manufacture, storage, distribution and transport or sale of tobacco, whether flavoured, scented or mixed with other ingredients such as nicotine, menthol etc.\" 8."
  },
